Playbook System Template
========================
Every Playbook System follows this standard structure to ensure reproducibility:

1. System Overview
   - Name and short narrative
   - Biological counterpart and clinical scenario

2. Roster Specification
   - Required archetypes (e.g., 1 Viral Hub, 1 Mutation Guard, 1 Immune Anchor, 2 Macrophages)
   - Parameter ranges for each archetype (e.g., Viral Load between X and Y; Mutation Complexity > threshold)

3. Metric Sheet
   - Formal definitions of all metrics in this system
   - References to Codex metrics: TER, Trueness, Flow, Gravity, Four Factors, DRtg, ORtg, Pace, Clutch Performance
   - New metrics specific to this system

4. Simulation Design
   - Time scale: possessions vs. cell cycles
   - State variables: score differential, tumor burden, immune activation, etc.
   - Update rules: who "acts" each tick and how metrics change

5. Experiment Examples
   - Suggested experiments (e.g., "knock out the endocrine hub and re-run," "increase immune coordination and observe regression")
   - How to log results in a standard format so different labs/teams can compare

6. Data Requirements
   - What datasets are needed (game logs, tracking data, clinical data, synthetic benchmarks)
   - How to format inputs for reproducibility

7. Validation Criteria
   - How to verify the system produces expected behavior
   - Baseline comparisons and known-good parameter sets

